Side-effects in the create flow: essentially none beyond persistence. There is NO event publishing (`ApplicationEventPublisher`), NO email/notification sending, and NO logging inside `addOwner` or `saveOwner`. The only logging in the whole path is in the exception advice (section 9). A monitoring aspect exists at `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/CallMonitoringAspect.java` (a general call-timing aspect over the service layer) — it is not owner-specific but would time the `ClinicService` calls. The response sets a `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header and returns `201 CREATED`.

No custom `Filter`/`HandlerInterceptor` is registered for this endpoint beyond the standard Spring Security filter chain above.

