## 9. Global exception handling — `@ControllerAdvice`

File: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`

Handlers relevant to owner creation:
- `MethodArgumentNotValidException` → 400 (Bean Validation failures from `@Valid OwnerFieldsDto`), builds a `ProblemDetail` with `schemaValidationErrors` and `errors` arrays (lines 133-168).
- `MissingOwnerFieldsException` → 400, body `{"errors": [<field names>]}` (lines 178-182).
- `InvalidTelephoneException` → 400, body `{"errors": ["telephone"]}` (lines 192-196).
- `InvalidEmailException` → 400, body `{"errors": ["email"]}` (lines 206-210).
- `DuplicateTelephoneException` → 409, body `{"errors": ["telephone"]}` (lines 220-224).
- `DuplicateHouseholdException` → 409, body `{"errors": ["lastName","address"]}` (lines 235-239).
- `DataIntegrityViolationException` → 404 (lines 113-124).
- `AccessDeniedException` → re-thrown so Spring Security produces 403/entry-point rather than 500 (lines 84-87).
- `Exception` (catch-all) → 500 `ProblemDetail` with logging (lines 96-103).

The custom exception classes (all `extends RuntimeException`) live in the same `rest/advice` package:
- `MissingOwnerFieldsException.java` — carries a `List<String> fields` (returned via `getFields()`).
- `InvalidEmailException.java`, `InvalidTelephoneException.java`, `DuplicateTelephoneException.java`, `DuplicateHouseholdException.java` — each a simple message-carrying `RuntimeException`.

